      "abstract": "THE FOLLOWING IS A SAMPLING of works useful for developing a critical perspective on mass culture and political consciousness under capitalism. This list is limited mainly to recent works, along with a few seminal earlier ones, and is meant to supplement, n.m supplant, the bibliographies in the many standard books on mass media, communication, and semantics, as well as sources such as Journal of Communication, Journal of Popular Culture, Journalism Quarterly, and the popular culture section in the Modern Language Association annual bibliography of English and American literature. Real's Mass-Mediated Culture and Sobel's The Manipulators provide thorough, up-to-date bibliographies, and Real presents, in his introductory and concluding chapters, a comprehensive survey of contemporary theories of mass culture including the Marxist perspective, which gets slighted in most standard American studies. A semi-annual bibliography, Marxism and the Mass Media, is published by International General, P. O. Box 350, New York, N. Y. 10013. Lee Baxandall's Marxism and Aesthetics: A Selective Annotated Bibliography (New York: Humanities Press, 1968) contains sections on theater, film, and dance. Two books published by the NCTE Committee on Public Doublespeak, Language and Public Policy, edited by Hugh Rank (Urbana: NCTE, 1974), and Teaching About Doublespeak, edited by Daniel Dieterich (Urbana: NCTE, 1976), are oriented toward English teachers and contain bibliographies of resources for classroom use.",
